+++ b/docs/collage-desktop-preview.md
@@ -0,0 +1,180 @@
+# Native Collages design preview
+
+The active V2 source now has a **Collages** tab beside school Composites and in
+the project workflow. Class composites keep their existing model, storage and
+production behavior. The native change has not been built, installed or released.
+
+## Implemented
+
+- Landscape three-portrait and portrait graduation presets match Cloud's
+  portable version 1 template. Openings can be added, removed and edited;
+  dimensions, borders, colours, caption positions, trim, bleed and safe inset
+  are editable.
+- Clean PNG/JPEG artwork overlays can contain transparent openings and logos.
+  A photograph of a finished collage remains a reference and does not remove
+  existing portraits or infer editable openings.
+- Local test photos can be reused, independently cropped and zoomed. Test-photo
+  assignments and student/school/year captions remain in memory. JSON exports
+  whitelist design fields and exclude these personal fields and local paths.
+- Each local save appends an immutable version in the signed-in photographer's
+  separate `collages/library.json`, using `AtomicJsonStore` and integrity hashes.
+  Owner/session changes stop pending actions; saved copies never modify older
+  versions.
+- Preview and PNG export share the native renderer and the exact Cloud source
+  crop calculation. Original-resolution images are normalized for EXIF
+  orientation before cropping. Low-resolution warnings use retained source
+  pixels per inch after the selected crop.
+- Native Cloud controls list/load immutable versions, save private drafts, and
+  open pricing and gallery publishing directly in the editor. The photographer
+  selects the price sheet, school/project galleries, standalone collage or
+  existing mixed package, total price per set and independent copies included.
+  They require the reviewed Cloud routes/migrations; the deployed server has not
+  been changed.
+- Native order-print preparation fetches each finished collage from the paid
+  Cloud production endpoint. It verifies exact order/item identity, authoritative
+  quantity, template and canonical recipe hashes, pixel dimensions and PNG hash.
+  It retains the original PNG and trim derivative in an owner-scoped cache with
+  a receipt. Cached files never authorize a later preparation without a fresh
+  paid-order request.
+
+## Print geometry
+
+`widthInches` and `heightInches` are the trim size. Output pixel dimensions are
+`round((trim + 2 × bleedInches) × 300)`. Normalized openings, artwork and caption
+coordinates are applied within the trim rectangle, offset by bleed. The paper
+colour fills the bleed. The artwork covers trim. Slot array order defines the
+photo layers, followed by artwork and then three caption lines. Borders are
+drawn inside their openings. The optional blue safe-inset guide is preview-only.
+
+PNG export is a print-sized **preview** and does not embed DPI metadata, apply a
+lab colour profile, place an order or send to a printer. Lab dimensions must be
+set explicitly. Pixel-identical text between Flutter and Cloud has not been
+verified across platforms; both specify Arial and use the same placement and
+horizontal fit rules.
+
+## Order compatibility and production
+
+Cloud `order_items.collage_snapshot` is retained as `collageSnapshot` in native
+order records. Separate collage copies never collapse by product/SKU/price;
+ordinary print rows retain their existing quantity-collapse behavior. A collage
+is multiple source photos inside one purchased print, never multiple print rows.
+
+Native Orders marks these items as collages and retains their immutable snapshot.
+Auto-match cannot replace the recipe with the student's first photo, a class
+composite or a manually chosen single photo. The legacy whole-order push also
+refuses to rewrite purchased collage recipes.
+
+The existing print preflight resolves each collage copy to its verified finished
+image. Native single-order and school-batch Noritsu preparation write one
+dedicated JPEG per purchased collage copy, at the exact trim pixels with 300 ppi
+metadata. They bypass portrait framing, Develop edits, backgrounds, GPU cropping
+and ganging. Ordinary print grouping is unchanged. Both original and trim PNG
+hashes, the immutable recipe and the current session are rechecked before any
+staged run is published. The existing payment/current-order preflight still runs
+at publication. Reprints perform a new authorized request.
+
+Bleed is retained in `original-with-bleed.png`; the lab JPEG uses
+`finished-trim.png`. If bleed falls on a half pixel, center trimming uses the
+nearest source-pixel boundary, with at most one pixel of asymmetric edge rounding.
+The integrity receipt records source and trim hashes and original source
+resolution-warning count.
+
+Native price pushes preserve the Cloud-owned item structure and category of a
+collage-containing product, including ordinary-print children in mixed packages.
+This protection survives repeated pushes after metadata baselines refresh; its
+deep copies cannot alias or mutate the Cloud snapshot. Normal three-way name,
+price and active-status merges continue, including existing price-conflict holds.
+Ordinary package item edits retain their previous merge behavior.
+
+The desktop editor now configures design-to-product bindings, total prices and
+gallery publication without opening a Cloud browser. The feature remains a
+preview; isolated tests simulate authentication, private storage and the payment
+provider and do not establish installed-app, Stripe test-mode or printer results. No customer data, installed app, production schema,
+payment-provider setting or automation setting was changed.
+
+## Desktop pricing and publication
+
+“Product/package price per set” is the total price for the whole product,
+including ordinary prints. “Collage copies included per set” creates independent
+physical collage copies. Parent purchase quantity multiplies complete sets;
+photo openings never become separate billable items. The publication summary
+shows the price sheet, selected galleries, preserved items and new collage copies.
+Existing packages can append a collage or replace one specific collage item,
+retaining ordinary prints, class composites and unrelated finish metadata.
+
+Decimal currency input is parsed directly to integer cents, with two fractional
+digits and no floating-point rounding. The server checks the current catalogue
+revision, owner, effective gallery price sheet, physical product and total price.
+One transaction saves a new immutable version, gallery access and the product
+binding. Each publication carries a durable request identity for idempotent retry.
+
+The owner-scoped `collages/commerce-pending.json` stores the exact reviewed body
+and integrity hash before sending. Lost responses and all HTTP errors retain it,
+including authentication, rate-limit and stale-catalogue races. Reopening the
+editor can retry the same request. A separate review action can explicitly remove
+only the local retry record after reviewing refreshed Cloud state; it never
+withdraws or deletes a Cloud product. Session changes block these actions.
+
+A confirmed receipt must match the reviewed photographer, currency, product,
+price sheet, total price, template/design/content hash, private artwork namespace,
+collage copy count, dimensions and every preserved package item. Crossed receipts
+cannot update local prices or clear the retry record. Matching local products are
+reconciled by Cloud identity; edits made locally during publication remain intact
+and retain their existing three-way conflict protection on later price pushes.
+
+Withdrawal revokes current gallery grants and preserves the immutable design and
+purchased snapshots. Refreshed availability counts distinguish active galleries
+from withdrawn versions; the immutable `published` flag alone is not availability.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run all desktop tests with `--dart-define=STUDIO_OS_EDITION=live-v2`. Focused
+tests cover portable-format validation and privacy, crop geometry, independent
+copies, mixed ordinary prints, immutable local saves, owner/session isolation,
+explicit private Cloud draft requests, native save/reload, narrow layout and
+EXIF-aware rendering with artwork, borders and bleed. Production fixtures pin a
+shared Cloud/Dart canonical hash, reject wrong order/item/template/recipe/quantity
+and pixel receipts, verify bleed trimming and whole-image JPEG output, preserve
+order records across preparation, and roll back staged output when verified
+pixels change before publication.
+
+Catalog fixtures also cover repeated native pushes, preservation of mixed-package
+collage configuration, unchanged ordinary edits and price-conflict handling.
+
+The default-concurrency suite initially had one existing mixed-order widget
+`pumpAndSettle` timeout, which passed in isolation. The final complete suite
+passed on the frozen isolated source with concurrency 2: **1,911 passed,
+4 skipped**. Static analysis covers the entire library, ten collage test files
+and the explicit fixture driver, with no issues. All **55 focused collage checks**
+pass across format, storage, native UI, rendering, Cloud requests, order
+compatibility, production, catalog sync and commerce. The four skips are optional
+roster/native-vision fixtures unavailable in this source-only copy; no collage
+test is skipped.
+
+Stage 2 adds commerce service and widget regressions for exact cents, legacy
+price-sheet identities, mixed-package replacement, concurrent preparations,
+persistent retries, crossed receipts, normalized private artwork, local price
+reconciliation, withdrawal/refresh and owner/session changes. The explicit
+`tool/collage_native_e2e_driver_test.dart` accepts a loopback fixture configuration
+through constructor injection; it does not change the installed backend. It has
+published a CAD 32.50 standalone set with two collages and a CAD 54.25 mixed
+5×7/two-collage set through the real API and SQL in the isolated Cloud harness.
+The parent browser purchased the exact mixed set, and the signed simulated-provider
+webhook marked that synthetic order paid. The native production phase then fetched
+its two independent collage recipes and staged two distinct 3000×2400 JPEGs through
+the existing Noritsu encoder. Original PNG hashes matched the Cloud receipts; final
+JPEG hashes and per-copy receipts are recorded. No printer was invoked. A read-only
+review phase captures the readable pricing/gallery/copy summary without publishing
+again.
+
+Concurrent work changed the active Orders editor during Stage 2. Those unrelated
+edits were preserved. Final tests use the separate runnable validation snapshot:
+the captured twenty-file baseline plus the nine commerce paths, with unrelated
+new watcher/auto-retouch tests excluded. Existing storage dependencies remain
+unchanged. A fresh read-only whole-library analysis of the active V2 source also
+passed with no issues after the concurrent edits progressed; its complete suite
+has not been rerun. The review commit contains only collage changes.
+
+`preview/collages-native-graduation.png` is a synthetic Flutter widget-test
+capture with a loaded Arial font. It is not proof of an installed-app or
+authenticated live-server workflow.
